{"formula": "=INDEX($B$2:$O$2,MATCH(1,INDEX(($B$3:$O$3=\"Velocity FPS\")*(INDEX($B:$O,D51,0)<>\"\")*(INDEX($B:$O,D51,0)<=$D$48),0),0))"}

Cell B17 should hold the years part of the average age. C17 already computes the months part as the average total months modulo 12, so B17 should be the integer part of the average total months divided by 12.

The formula mirrors C17's structure:

{"formula": "=INT(((SUM(B2:B7)*12+SUM(C2:C7))/ROWS(A2:A7))/12)"}

B26 is the TOTAL WEIGHT for angler 1. B25 holds total ounces, so the weight in pounds is B25 divided by 16. Since the intent is somewhat ambiguous, the most likely choice is converting the ounces back to pounds.

Alternatively, A21+B21/16 would give the same result, but B25/16 is simpler.

