{"formula": "=SUMIF(M44:M112,\">0\")/ABS(SUMIF(M44:M112,\"<0\"))"}

The cell next to "MSE =" in I16 is J16, so the formula should be the mean squared error between the actual sales (B) and the forecast (G). Forecasts start at G6 and actuals run through B15, so the matching range is rows 6 to 15.

SUMXMY2 returns the sum of squared differences, and dividing by the count gives the MSE.

{"formula": "=SUMXMY2(B6:B15,G6:G15)/COUNT(G6:G15)"}

The Logged Time column (J) should hold only the time-of-day from the logged-in timestamp in column B. The other formulas compare J to A, where A is a pure time, so J needs to strip the date.

`=MOD(B2,1)` returns just the time portion of B2.

