The Earliest Date Attended column should take the minimum of the date columns C, E, G and I. Those cells hold either a number or an empty string (""), and MIN ignores text in references, so it works directly. If no dates exist, MIN returns 0, so I'll wrap it in an IF to return blank in that case.

A non-contiguous range works with MIN(C2,E2,G2,I2), and wrapping it in IF handles the all-blank case.

{"formula": "=IF(COUNT(C2,E2,G2,I2)=0,\"\",MIN(C2,E2,G2,I2))"}

Column H ("Health Ins. Deduction") most likely mirrors the rate lookup in column G, but pulls from the payroll-deduction table in O:U. That table has Employee and Dependent columns for each of the three plans, with ages in column U. Here is the formula I'd expect:

{"formula": "=IF(ISNUMBER(D5),INDEX(IF(E5=\"Y\",CHOOSE(D5,$P$8:$P$73,$R$8:$R$73,$T$8:$T$73),CHOOSE(D5,$O$8:$O$73,$Q$8:$Q$73,$S$8:$S$73)),MATCH(C5,$U$8:$U$73,0)),0)"}

